<x-filament-panels::page>
    <div class="tala-prose">
        <h2>Native structure, TALA appearance</h2>
        <p>This sample uses Filament’s supported sidebar-only arrangement: the topbar is disabled through panel configuration, and the theme control uses the sidebar-footer render hook. Desktop collapse, the mobile menu trigger and drawer, forms, records table, dialogs, and notifications retain native behavior. Semantic color palettes, local Inter typography, and subtle button lighting supply the visual identity.</p>
        <h2>Compact through configuration</h2>
        <p>The sidebar width is configured through the panel API. The form uses a native compact section and responsive columns. There is no hover expansion, sidebar resizing, custom mobile bottom navigation, or scroll-hiding script.</p>
        <h2>Adapt according to role</h2>
        <p>Filled buttons receive restrained lighting. Outlined, link, selected, loading, disabled, and focus states keep their native meaning. Native Heroicons remain the icon set here.</p>
        <h2>Requirements select the examples</h2>
        <p>PRDs and the UI Blueprint determine fields, permissions, workflows, and authoritative records. These fictional examples demonstrate styling and composition without defining school policy or a global staff dashboard.</p>
        <h2>Use the design skills appropriately</h2>
        <p>Use Better Layout for grouping and responsive composition, Better UI for surface consistency, and the relevant typography, color, writing, and accessibility skills for their disciplines. Use Impeccable’s relevant playbooks and detector as quality checks within the native framework and approved visual direction.</p>
        <div class="tala-actions">
            <x-filament::button href="/public" tag="a" color="gray">View Bootstrap example</x-filament::button>
            <x-filament::button href="http://127.0.0.1:4173/experimental.html#projects" tag="a" color="gray" outlined>Explore earlier experiments</x-filament::button>
        </div>
    </div>
</x-filament-panels::page>
